{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/671488-return-of-the-white-howlers-and-pentex-bsd-falling-out","id":671488,"title":"Return of the White Howlers and Pentex/BSD falling out?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-19T17:04:42-07:00","id":671488,"title":"Return of the White Howlers and Pentex/BSD falling out?","content":"An idea I had, is of the 3 options for return of the White howlers...The great quest is by far my favorite, spontaneous rebirth just feels wrong and &quot;Never fell&quot; Just ruins too much off the cosmology, to be worthwhile.with my understanding of what a garou tribe is. is a Falling out with Pentex a particularly bad way to go about it?<br /> <br /> With the BSD's former allys turning on them, their would probaly be 3 or 4 who wound up winding up in Erebus... not sure why logically, it just seems like a compelling combination of events.<br /> <br /> Maybe one of the Dancer Packs totem spirit spontaneously redeems from their desperate courage<br /> <br /> (In the Werewolf storytellers guide, I think it lists &quot;Redeem a bane without gifts&quot; as a suitable Quest for a rank 5 theruge, so clearly it is POSSIBLE<br /> <br /> <br /> I get its an unlikely and tenuous connection but I just find it a compelling combination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-19-2015, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T16:09:06-07:00","id":672454,"title":"","content":"So if I understand you your idea is<br /> <br /> Pentex turns against the Black Spiral Dancers or the contrary (both are possible as Pentex openly attempts to replace the Dancers with Mockeries)<br /> <br /> The Dancers lose the war (Why not Pentex knows some of the Tribe's secrets and their Fomorii are at home in Pits)<br /> <br /> ???<br /> <br /> White Howlers reborn.<br /> <br /> There's a few ways to do that<br /> <br /> 1 With the Tribe embroiled in a deadly war against the might of Pentex,some cubs are not initiated in the Black Spiral. They could be survivors of an attack against a Pit. Toddlers and children deposed by BSD's parents in a Caern's bawn in an uncharacteristic display of love.<br /> <br /> 2 Pentex is decisevely winning the war, some adult BSD's come crying to the Garou for protection. While many will be sumarly killed by the Ga\u00efans I expect some Children of Ga\u00efa Septs at the least offer asylum, the time to throw the BSD's in Erebus.<br /> <br /> 3 Not directly related to your thing. Bat was canonly redeemed at least partialy by the Shadow Lords. You can say it redeemed itself fully and brings its bastards with it.<br /> <br /> Of course none of these options gets you White Howlers. For that you must persuade Lion's to give his patronage to a Tribe's once more. (and even that IMHO wouldn't bring the Howlers' back, they had a very distinctive culture with notably links to wraiths that is not repleaceale in the modern day)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T21:43:56-07:00","id":672879,"title":"","content":"Yes but its listed as a possiblety in the tribebook<br /> <br /> And lions patronage WOULD get you the gifts back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T11:48:06-07:00","id":673320,"title":"","content":"It's stated in the howler tribe book that lion would take notice of a new howler. He apparently wants to be a totem again (go figure huh?), with the major opposition being the talons and griffin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T12:19:27-07:00","id":673343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/671488-return-of-the-white-howlers-and-pentex-bsd-falling-out?p=672879#post672879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but its listed as a possiblety in the tribebook<br /> <br /> And lions patronage WOULD get you the gifts back.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have to agree with Ganonso. Lion did not teach all of the White Howler gifts. He had a brood of spirits when they existed and his brood aided him and his patrons. Many Lion's brood serve the Wyrm now or have faded into obscurity, some of which have not been seen since the fall. I think in Lion's diminished capacity he in fact would not be able to offer them the gift selection he used to be able to offer them.<br /> <br /> That said there are two options for a White Howler return that the books have talked about. There is a White Howler mentioned in the Tribe book who can not die, he is protected by a spirit. Currently he is frozen in an iceberg Captain America-style somewhere in the northern hemisphere. Due to the temperature shift he may thaw out or he may simply be found by the players due to a quest from Lion, or both. In any case his return would give the new howlers a legitimate White Howler Elder to follow.<br /> <br /> The second option is talked about in the new Umbra book. There is a White Howler wraith haunting the Dark umbra, hunting down BSD that are unlucky enough to cross his path. He is the spirit of the only White Howler to escape Malfeas the night the tribe fell. He is probably the only legitimate White Howler ancestor spirit left. If he could over come his grief in some way and ascend to true Ancestor Spirit then he would be able to help teach the new howlers some of the old gifts.<br /> <br /> I have been working on a story based around their return and ideally the story for reforming the Howler's would happen in 3 acts:<br /> <br /> Act 1: Mantle of the Lion - Gain Lion's patronage. Not an easy task because he has moved on and it part of Griffon's Brood. To leave would be a great dishonor to the spirit that saved him. This could potentially gain the new tribe hostility from the Red Talons moving forward. If he is to take on there patronage he has the new pack take on an insurmountable task: Locate Eubh &quot;The Ever-Living&quot; and return him to Lion.<br /> <br /> Act 2: Return of the King - Find Eubh &quot;The Ever-Living&quot;. They will be in the frozen north where only Wendigo, Crazy Red Talons, and Ice Stalkers roam. He is always protected by the spirit of the White Wolf (Mother Wolf), so she may guide them to his resting place and they need to find a way to recover his frozen body for White Wolf to bring back. If they succeed then they should return with Eubh to Lion.<br /> <br /> Act 3: Spirits of the Past - Find the lost spirit of the last White Howler in the dark umbra. Lion is impressed by their tenacity but does not feel they have what it takes to be true howlers.. yet. His next task for them is to find the spirit of the last howler to survive and return him to Eubh and Lion so that he may be brought back into the fold. Obviously a dangerous in it own right to go into the dark umbra. When they find him he is surrounded by the souls of all the Garou he has 'freed' from the Wyrm. It will not be an easy sell, his self loathing for the fall of his tribe and his own initial survival makes returning to the fold a traumatizing endeavor.<br /> <br /> Given that the players succeed in all of the tasks above they have all of the cultural and spiritual resources to rebuild the tribe. To continue the story I would move on to rebuilding Lion's brood and rebuilding their numbers. I would use totems from the tribe book that have not fallen as the base for rebuilding the brood then as the players grow in rank, move on to purifying totems that have fallen. Rebuilding numbers would come in the form finding lost kinfolk and bringing them into the fold or finding Ronin who are looking for a cause and trying to get them to join. This could bring them into direct conflict with the Skin Dancers which might be an interesting side story for the players if they have never dealt with them before.<br /> <br /> The last part is not so much a single story line as much as many individual story lines that would make up an entire game over time. Again this is just something I have been working on, you can do it any way you think best, and obviously this is not a single quest and magically they return. This is a entire story that effectively brings them to modern day in a new incarnation using ancient assets that still exist in cannon. There is a lot of play and storytelling required to do it my way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T19:32:50-07:00","id":673766,"title":"","content":"And don't forget that W20 has a BSD stuck in the silver sea of Erebus for ten years now, slowly being purified though no one knows if or when that will happen. Though it has been drifting back to shore as of late...<br /> <br /> I would also bring up the ending of <i>Rage Across Australia </i>but that's rather wonky ending in a wonky book so I'd ignore that or at least take it with a grain of salt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T06:06:49-07:00","id":674081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/671488-return-of-the-white-howlers-and-pentex-bsd-falling-out?p=673766#post673766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And don't forget that W20 has a BSD stuck in the silver sea of Erebus for ten years now, slowly being purified though no one knows if or when that will happen. Though it has been drifting back to shore as of late...<br /> <br /> I would also bring up the ending of <i>Rage Across Australia </i>but that's rather wonky ending in a wonky book so I'd ignore that or at least take it with a grain of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Both scenario's only cleanse the existing BSD of their taint. It does not supply them with the Spiritual or Cultural knowledge to actually become White Howlers. They are effectively Ronin with no Rank and access to no gifts at all as the cleansing process strips them of all gifts granted by the wyrm, or at least that is what Erebus used to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T07:33:59-07:00","id":674187,"title":"","content":"Indeed it does, but if they're willing to become howlers again, it is written in tribe book that lion WILL notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T07:43:30-07:00","id":674194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/671488-return-of-the-white-howlers-and-pentex-bsd-falling-out?p=674187#post674187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed it does, but if they're willing to become howlers again, it is written in tribe book that lion WILL notice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So you could work that into the rebuilding the numbers story. Have the new pack venture into Erebus to request the punishment rite from Charyss herself. Then they can go around and send BSD to Erebus to be cleansed and then redeem them afterwards. <br /> <br /> The new Howlers return and subsequent hunting of the BSD could be why the BSD have their falling out with Pentex. While they are busy dealing with the new Howler's this could be the opportunity in story for the Mockeries to start taking over their function in the company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T18:34:57-07:00","id":674774,"title":"","content":"Iirc, haven't the BSD taken so many kidnap victims and made them walk the spiral that they are no longer really White Howlers even by blood at this point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T19:08:48-07:00","id":674794,"title":"","content":"There are a small number of them that still carry the blood line, this is reflected on their Pure Breed ban where they can only take it at level 5. That said not all of their kin was subjugated by the BSD, the books talk about them taking refuge with other tribes, so their blood exists outside of the BSD in the tribes like the Fianna. Blood really plays very little in the way of determining ones tribe. I don't have the source at hand but i remember reading in one of the books that a garou's parents could be of one tribe but when it comes time for him to go through the rite of passage he could be rejected by the tribal totem and taken in by the spirits of another tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T13:29:16-07:00","id":676800,"title":"","content":"I agree withDerhuzad on blood determining tribe, just look at the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers, their defining feature is that they don't have any Pure Breed to speak of. While some Garou of a high Pure Breed rating will be leaned upon rather heavily to join a specific tribe, it's clearly not the only determining factor. Black Furies give away male cubs but they demand the ability to recruit female cubs from other tribes in return. Pure Breed and family tradition plays a pretty heavy role in the tribe a cub joins but I also feel that there are quite a few lost cubs out there who are of an indeterminate tribe and they join the one they align with ideologically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T10:04:06-07:00","id":677745,"title":"","content":"Don't know how kosher or not would it be for you people's games, but i do remember an old Werewolf campaign where the PCs pack, in one of their repeated trips to the Abyss to get revenge on Nightmaster (messy story) came across a White Howler that was sort of petrified there in a time before the tribe's fall and was inadvertently freed amidst their chaotic, insane, brutal fighting of the pack in the damn place and kind of followed them out and back to the world, where they would try to help him to more or less sort out things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:19:09-07:00","id":677916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/671488-return-of-the-white-howlers-and-pentex-bsd-falling-out?p=677745#post677745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know how kosher or not would it be for you people's games, but i do remember an old Werewolf campaign where the PCs pack, in one of their repeated trips to the Abyss to get revenge on Nightmaster (messy story) came across a White Howler that was sort of petrified there in a time before the tribe's fall and was inadvertently freed amidst their chaotic, insane, brutal fighting of the pack in the damn place and kind of followed them out and back to the world, where they would try to help him to more or less sort out things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you remember the source?<br /> <br /> I was doing some reading and there was a pure breed white howler born and managed to escape the BSD before they got to him (thanks to Samual Haight of all people). Though he's technically a Ronin for all intents and purposes but he adds just one more part to the recruit plan. Hell I might even work it in that he is the character driving the story line and adding a trip to the abyss sounds like fun lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T23:45:40-07:00","id":678594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/671488-return-of-the-white-howlers-and-pentex-bsd-falling-out?p=677916#post677916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you remember the source?<br /> <br /> I was doing some reading and there was a pure breed white howler born and managed to escape the BSD before they got to him (thanks to Samual Haight of all people). Though he's technically a Ronin for all intents and purposes but he adds just one more part to the recruit plan. Hell I might even work it in that he is the character driving the story line and adding a trip to the abyss sounds like fun lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>No particular source, the White Howler per se was totally the ST's creation afaik, but i felt the idea of the Abyss as somewhere in the Umbra where remnants, living or not, of past ages might be lost or imprisoned due to that place's nature seemed worth mentioning and thematic to the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T06:22:25-07:00","id":685629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/671488-return-of-the-white-howlers-and-pentex-bsd-falling-out?p=678594#post678594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No particular source, the White Howler per se was totally the ST's creation afaik, but i felt the idea of the Abyss as somewhere in the Umbra where remnants, living or not, of past ages might be lost or imprisoned due to that place's nature seemed worth mentioning and thematic to the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a great idea, thank you for sharing. Adds a little more to the story I am working on. I love incorporating parts of Umbra that Garou don't normally travel to. It just feels even more thematic for a White Howler revival because that was what got them in trouble in the first place lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}